id: pm-fo8g7j
title: Unknown-option refusals identify the actual rejected flag and fail closed at delimiters
description: "A real invocation of pm search with the unsupported --include-body option emits code=unknown_option and correctly names --include-body in its title/detail, but refusal.surface is --status because the shared envelope builder selects the first provided field. That machine-readable contradiction sends SDK, MCP, and CLI agents toward a valid option instead of the rejected one and undermines recovery-closure scoring. Derive the refused surface and rejected value from the actual unknown-option diagnostic while preserving redaction and fallback behavior."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",contracts,recovery,structured-errors
created_at: "2026-08-27T16:23:50.108Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T09:01:36.449Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-28T09:01:35.892Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-28T09:01:35.892Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "unknown_option refusal.surface equals the actual rejected option regardless of valid options that precede it; refusal.rejected_value and recovery metadata remain internally consistent and redaction-safe; CLI JSON, SDK normalization, and executable recovery-corpus tests cover mixed valid-plus-unknown option orderings; The regression is represented in task-transcript and refusal-closure assurance"
parent: pm-f05lsg
resolution: Canonicalize inline provided-field fallbacks before refusal attribution so the shared resolver publishes the flag identity and rejected scalar consistently.
expected_result: Every invalid-domain refusal exposes a canonical flag surface and the rejected inline value even when prose does not name the flag.
actual_result: "Inline --depth=verbose fallback now emits surface --depth, rejected_value verbose, the complete legal domain, and exit code 2 across unit and black-box CLI paths."
